{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה.</b> What does this come to tell us — was Esau in doubt about his blessing? Therefore one must say that what he said, ״אֹרְרֶיךָ אָרוּר״ (Genesis 27:29), means: if you curse others, I will agree with you, such that whoever you curse shall be cursed; and likewise ״מְבָרְכֶיךָ״ — whomever you bless, I will agree to your blessing, that he shall be blessed; for he had delivered blessings into his hand to bless whomever he wishes. And concerning this Isaac said ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״ — not only have I blessed him already, but I even said to him ״וֶהְיֵה בְרָכָה״ (Genesis 12:2), and I gave into his hand to bless whomever he wishes; and after I have delivered the blessings into his hand, how can I take back from his hand what I have already given him? And what does it avail that I bless you if he does not agree with me? Accordingly, ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״ is from the expression ״וֶהְיֵה בְרָכָה״. And do not answer me from the וָי״ו of ״בָּרוּךְ״, whose meaning would be that he shall be blessed [passively]: we find a precedent for this, that our Sages of blessed memory expounded (Sotah 38b): one does not give the cup of blessing except to one of goodly eye, as it is stated (Proverbs 22:9) ״טוֹב עַיִן הוּא יְבֹרָךְ״ — do not read ״יְבֹרָךְ״ but ״יְבָרֵךְ״." "Another matter: therefore he said ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״, lest Esau say: surely Jacob's blessing is not eternal, and you will be able to interpret your words to mean that Jacob's blessing shall take effect for a fixed time, and when his time is finished, Esau's blessings will begin. Concerning this he said ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״ — not only do I bless him in the present, but ״גַּם בָּרוּךְ יִהְיֶה״, meaning, it shall be so forever; and if so, there is no room for your blessings to take effect, neither in the present nor in the future. And Esau said ״הֲלֹא אָצַלְתָּ לִּי בְרָכָה״ — do you not have another blessing set aside for me like it? And is it not possible for two blessings to take effect simultaneously? And he answered him, ״הֵן גְּבִיר שַׂמְתִּיו לָךְ״ — and what a servant acquires, his master acquires, and if so, what can be given to him? And because of his insistent pleading, he gave room for his blessing to take effect, saying ״וְהָיָה כַּאֲשֶׁר תָּרִיד״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:39.157384753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}